      "subhead": "Patient monitoring pulse oximeter",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-e2eca0ceb5@example.invalid",
      "imageAlt": "spo2",
      "jcr:created": "Tue Mar 25 2025 22:21:17 GMT+0000",
      "headColor": "rgb(255,181,0)",
      "head": "<p>Reprocessed Masimo LNCS®  pulse oximeter sensors</p>\r\n",
      "content": "The Masimo LNCS pulse oximeter sensors are a noninvasive device attached to a patient’s fingertip, toe or foot and emits light through the appendage to consistently monitor blood oxygen saturation. LNCS, or low noise cabled sensors are available in a large variety of sizes and designs to fit several patient needs. Features and benefits include:\r\n\r\n\r\n<ul><li>Variety of traditional cable lengths</li><li>Connector positioned away from the sensor application site</li><li>Appropriate for short or long-term patient monitoring</li><li>Minimizes the rise of HAI or cross-contamination</li></ul>\r\n\r\nSustainability Solutions offers single use reprocessed Masimo LNCS pulse oximeter devices in both transpore and woven styles for adult, pediatric and infant patients.\r\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Mar 25 2025 22:24:00 GMT+0000",
      "compImageRef": "/content/dam/stryker/endoscopy/products/masimo-lncs/images/Reprocessed Masimo 1859 Pulse Oximeter Sensor.png",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/hero",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    }
  },
